!YSFlight - M1 test build
=========================

This is NOT the game yet. It is the YSFlight Community Edition console
server (no window, no graphics, no sound), built for RISC OS to check that
the simulator core works: loading the aircraft, maps and start positions,
and flying the AI traffic.

Needs: SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and ARMEABISupport (PackMan).
PThreadTicker 0.03 is included and loaded by !Run.

Double-click !YSFlight. A task window opens and runs, showing the
output in the window (each list should take seconds):
  1. the aircraft list        (NAIR:88; 176 is also fine)
  2. the map list             (NFLD:18; 36 is also fine)
  3. Aomori start positions   (NSTP:36)
  4. Hawaii start positions   (NSTP:56)
  5. the server. It prints "Thread 0 ready." to "Thread 3 ready."
     (its 4 threads have started), then "Ready to go!", then messages about AI
     aircraft taxiing and landing. Leave it a few minutes, then press
     Escape.
Each step's error output goes to a file in Logs (AircraftE ...
ServerE). If the program crashes, that file has the RISC OS error and a
backtrace.

Settings are saved in <Choices$Write>.YSFlight.

Please report: the task window's text (Save from its menu), the files
in Logs, and any error box, with its exact text.

This is an unofficial port, not made or supported by the YSCE
developers. AI (Anthropic's Claude) has been used as a coding assistant.

